{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-011", "score": 0.165, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-011 | Study family SF-APPS-011: Regular season vs playoff PPP by play type (DRIVE over-prediction)\n- observed_research_question: Regular season vs playoff PPP by play type (DRIVE over-prediction)\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: DRIVE PPP is materially higher in RS than playoffs, so an RS-calibrated optimizer over-recommends DRIVE.\n- observed_result: DRIVE RS 1.198 vs PO 0.912 (-0.286, 25 teams); PNR -0.173; PULL_UP +0.301; others within -0.07.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: DRIVE playoff PPP 0.286 below RS across 25 teams; top-10 teams all -0.30 to -0.43.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 25 teams, min 30 poss per cell; no CIs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Team-level (team, PT, context) cells, min 30 poss, up to 25 teams.\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- observed_failure_type: D_positive\n- observed_notes: Motivated the playoff DRIVE exclusion and a proposed playoff DSI offset."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-032", "score": 0.095, "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-032 | Study family SF-PAP-032: Travel x fit screen vs real player outcomes (minutes, usage, net rating)\n- observed_research_question: Travel x fit screen vs real player outcomes (minutes, usage, net rating)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: The travel x fit quadrant (additive vs redundant/missed-need/irrelevant) predicts post-move minutes, usage, and destination on-court net rating.\n- observed_result: n=198; embedded mpg>=15: additive 0.80, redundant 0.85, missed-need 0.50, irrelevant 0.68; mean dest net: additive -0.63, redundant -0.35, missed-need -2.50, irrelevant -3.58; corr(delta, dest_net)=+0.077; corr(travel_sc [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL\n- observed_failure_evidence: net-rating gap additive vs irrelevant is large but corr(delta, dest_net)=+0.077; fit_score correlations are negative; in-sample thresholds\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=198 movers"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-039", "score": 0.094, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPM-039 | Study family SF-APPM-039: Travel x fit screen and outcome holdout validation\n- observed_research_question: Travel x fit screen and outcome holdout validation\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Forecast portability (travel) and fit quadrants predict mover outcomes (embedded minutes, net rating).\n- observed_result: LOO corr 0.1998, AUC 0.5986; holdout additive embedded 89.59% vs irrelevant 48.11%; P(add emb > irr)=0.984; P(add net > irr)=0.99; corr(travel,net) 0.1881.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Additive > irrelevant in 98.4% of splits.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=230\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPM-039: 'utcomes); loo travel forecast; 500 random 50/50 calibration/holdout splits. loo corr 0.1998, auc 0.5986; holdout additive embed'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-033\n- observed_method: 296 movers (230 with outcomes); LOO travel forecast; 500 random 50/50 calibration/holdout splits."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-016", "score": 0.092, "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-016 | Study family SF-PAP-016: Portability feasibility gate\n- observed_research_question: Portability feasibility gate\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Enough movers with decoys exist and displacement signature is not collinear with play-type profile.\n- observed_result: Prereg: 296 movers, decoy frac 1.00, vacuity rho=0.048; final output: 294 movers, rho=0.007\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: gate passed\n- observed_sample_and_power: 296/294 movers\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF19\n- observed_method: Mover signature cache; G1 >=25 movers, G2 >=80% with >=3 decoys, G3 |rho|<0.90.\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- observed_failure_type: D_positive\n- observed_notes: Mover count and vacuity rho changed between prereg record and final output.\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)\n- auto_addresses_question: RQC:RQC-051\n- auto_uses_method: METH:correlation"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
